.TH SCRNCAPTURE 1
.SH NAME
scrncapture \- capture the screen to a file and back
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/scrncapture
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ScrnCapture
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/ScrnCapture.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Take a picture, put it in a file, and paint the file back.  The
original's comment points at how Stadium's background was made: capture a
drawing once, ship the capture.
.PP
An Inferno program can read only the pixels of its own window, so this
captures the window rather than the display.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Capture, then read back, then exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/scrncapture.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/$user/demoscrnshot
The capture, in the format
.IR image (6)
describes.
